From: ACloudViewer downstream
Subject: [PATCH] Type-differentiated CUDA Q8_1 sum semantics (MMQ standard for Q4_1/Q5_1, raw for Q4_K/Q5_K)

block_q8_1.s is defined in ggml-common.h as "d * sum(qs[i])" - the sum of
the DEQUANTIZED activations - and quantize_row_q8_1_ref (CPU) plus the CPU
vec_dot_q4_1_q8_1 / vec_dot_q5_1_q8_1 (m_x * s_y) correction consumers all
follow that definition. The upstream CUDA quantize kernels stored the RAW
float activation sum instead, so every Q4_0/Q4_1/Q5_0/Q5_1 mul_mat
correction term diverged between CPU and CUDA:

  - MMVQ (quantize_q8_1): raw float sum.
  - MMQ  (quantize_mmq_q8_1, DS4 layout used by Q4_1/Q5_1/Q4_K/Q5_K): raw
    float sum.

Measured with identical weights/activations (K=1024, N=3072, M=257,
activation mean 1.0 so the m-term matters): CPU-vs-CUDA Q4_1 mul_mat
max_abs error drops from 0.658 to 0.044 and Q4_0 from 0.627 to 0.046 -
both now at the pure int32-accumulation rounding level. End-to-end on
sam3-visual-q4_1 (cand1.jpg, RTX 3060): q4_1-CUDA vs f16-CUDA mask IoU
improves 0.978 -> 0.994.

Type differentiation is required because the two DS4 consumers disagree:

  - Q4_1/Q5_1 (MMQ DS4): quantize_mmq_q8_1 is instantiated with
    standard_sum=true, storing s = d * sum(qs[i]) to keep the CPU parity
    above (SAM3 q4_1 backend-parity gate).
  - Q4_K/Q5_K (MMQ DS4): standard_sum=false keeps the upstream raw float
    sum. Their correction consumer vec_dot_q4_K_q8_1_impl_mmq reads
    ds8.y for sumf_m = ds8.y * m[i], and the sam-3d-objects-ggml
    reference (v0.21.0 base + their patch) computes it with the raw sum:
    standardizing it broke sam3d q4_k conditioning parity (DINO block-0
    qkv projection diverged at int8-quantization scale, amplified by the
    pinned-noise e2e into a ~0.2% gaussian-count gap).
  - D2S6 (Q2_K): raw sum, unchanged from upstream.
  - MMVQ k-quant kernels consume the int8 dot (dot2), not ds.y, so the
    quantize_q8_1 change is neutral for them and stays standard for the
    Q4_1/Q5_1 MMVQ correction.

--- a/src/ggml-cuda/quantize.cu
+++ b/src/ggml-cuda/quantize.cu
@@ -83,21 +83,29 @@
     ggml_cuda_pdl_sync();
     const float xi = i0 < ne00 ? x[i03*s03 + i02*s02 + i01*s01 + i00] : 0.0f;
     float amax = fabsf(xi);
-    float sum = xi;
 
     amax = warp_reduce_max<QK8_1>(amax);
-    sum  = warp_reduce_sum<QK8_1>(sum);
 
     const float  d = amax / 127.0f;
     const int8_t q = amax == 0.0f ? 0 : roundf(xi / d);
 
     y[ib].qs[iqs] = q;
 
+    // Standard block_q8_1 semantics (ggml-common.h): s = d * sum(qs[i]) -
+    // the dequantized activation sum, matching quantize_row_q8_1_ref on the
+    // CPU and the MMQ DS4 standard_sum instantiation. Storing the raw float
+    // sum here made the Q4_1/Q5_1 correction term m_x * s_y diverge between
+    // the CPU and CUDA (SAM3 backend-parity mask IoU 0.977 vs the 0.98
+    // gate). The k-quant MMVQ consumers read the int8 dot, not ds.y, so the
+    // change is neutral for them.
+    float sumq = (float) q;
+    sumq = warp_reduce_sum<QK8_1>(sumq);
+
     if (iqs > 0) {
         return;
     }
 
-    y[ib].ds = make_half2(d, sum);
+    y[ib].ds = make_half2(d, d * sumq);
 }
 
